@model bool
@*
    The replay stage: the map, its chrome, and the pull-up dock under it.

    Shared by BOTH pages that show a race — the owner's /Races/Replay and the public /s/{token} fork —
    because they render the identical stage and only differ in what lives AROUND it (the owner page adds
    the Sections editor, the rider panels and the Share button; the fork adds none of them). The TS side
    was unified first (race-sim/race-replay-view.ts); this is the Razor half of the same discipline, so a
    change to the stage lands once instead of twice.

    The model is one bool: whether the viewer may edit. It reaches the profile's aria-label through the
    strip partial — the click-to-place behaviour itself is gated in race-replay-view (editable:false on
    the fork).

    The fullscreen button expands THIS whole block; a class flips it to fill the viewport. Everything but
    the map is chrome that overlays it, in both states.
*@
<div class="race-hero" id="raceHero">
    <div class="race-map-wrap">
        <div id="raceMap" class="race-map"></div>

        @* Manual fullscreen — Play stays inline; this is the only thing that goes fullscreen. *@
        <button id="raceMapFullscreen" type="button" class="race-map-expand" title="Fullscreen replay" aria-label="Fullscreen replay">
            <i class="bi bi-arrows-fullscreen"></i>
        </button>

        <div id="raceLoading" class="race-loading">Loading the field…</div>
        @* A replay that cannot load must SAY so — it used to sit on "Loading the field…" forever. *@
        <div id="raceError" class="race-error alert alert-danger" role="alert" hidden></div>

        @* Follow sidebar + fullscreen close button. *@
        <partial name="/Pages/Races/_RaceReplayOverlay.cshtml" />

        @* The shared dock — [grip][transport][charts] as one stack over the map's bottom edge. It
           OVERLAYS the map rather than sitting under it: as a sibling below the map the grip belonged to
           neither the bar nor the charts, and the map's bottom edge left a dead band between them. *@
        <partial name="/Pages/Shared/_ReplayDock.cshtml" model="@(new ReplayDockModel(
            DockId: "raceChartsDrawer",
            HandleId: "raceChartsHandle",
            StripId: "raceCharts",
            ControlsId: "raceReplayControls",
            PlayPauseId: "raceReplayPlayPause",
            SeekId: "raceReplaySeek",
            CurrentTimeId: "raceReplayCurrentTime",
            SpeedSlowerId: "raceReplaySpeedSlower",
            SpeedLabelId: "raceReplaySpeedLabel",
            SpeedFasterId: "raceReplaySpeedFaster",
            SpeedSelectId: "raceReplaySpeed")
        {
            StripClass = "race-charts",
            StripPartial = "/Pages/Races/_RaceChartsStrip.cshtml",
            StripPartialModel = Model,
            // The race opens paused, and its speed ladder is scaled to the event's duration — neither the
            // play icon nor "1x" would be true here.
            StartsPlaying = false,
            SpeedLabelText = "--",
        })" />
    </div>
</div>
